{"pageWidth":585,"pageHeight":783,"items":[{"text":"CLINICAL STATEMENTS","rect":[565.4300000000001,631.5849999999996,576.4300000000001,713.9134],"fontSize":11},{"text":"AND GUIDELINES","rect":[554.4300000000001,640.4949999999997,565.4300000000001,702.4195000000001],"fontSize":11},{"text":"Stroke.","rect":[49.5,24.712999999999997,73.05199999999999,32.712999999999994],"fontSize":8},{"text":"2026;57:e316–e436. DOI: 10.1161/STR.0000000000000513","rect":[75.22000000000001,24.712999999999997,291.31439999999986,32.712999999999994],"fontSize":8},{"text":"August 2026","rect":[460.6727,24.712999999999997,505.3367,32.712999999999994],"fontSize":8},{"text":"e317","rect":[517.3367,24.712999999999997,535.4966999999999,32.712999999999994],"fontSize":8},{"text":"Prabhakaran et al","rect":[49,749.74,107.85600000000002,757.74],"fontSize":8},{"text":"2026 Acute Ischemic Stroke Guideline","rect":[405.328,749.74,534.9992,757.74],"fontSize":8},{"text":"AIM:","rect":[49.5,713.785,65.137,723.285],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"The “2026 Guideline for the Early Management of Patients With AIS” replaces the “2018 Guidelines for the Early","rect":[68.595,713.785,535.44305,723.285],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"Management of Patients With AIS” and the 2019 update to reflect recent advances in evidence. This updated guideline","rect":[49.5,702.784,535.4629999999997,712.284],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"is intended to provide a comprehensive, up-to-date, evidence-based set of recommendations, advising management from","rect":[49.5,691.783,535.5010000000007,701.283],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"prehospital evaluation through acute treatment and early in-hospital management of complications and initiation of early","rect":[49.5,680.782,535.52,690.282],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"secondary prevention measures. The intended audience includes prehospital care professionals, physicians, allied health","rect":[49.5,669.7810000000001,535.4829500000001,679.2810000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"professionals, and hospital administrators.","rect":[49.5,658.7800000000001,213.80250000000004,668.2800000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"METHODS:","rect":[49.5,639.7800000000001,85.56105,649.2800000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"A search for literature derived from research principally involving human subjects, published in English since the","rect":[88.374,639.7800000000001,535.5532500000002,649.2800000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"last AIS guideline in 2018 and the 2019 update, and indexed in MEDLINE, PubMed, Cochrane Library, and other selected","rect":[49.5,628.7790000000001,535.5048000000002,638.2790000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"databases relevant to this guideline, was conducted between September and December 2024. Additional high impact studies","rect":[49.5,617.7780000000001,535.4725000000003,627.2780000000001],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"and articles published through March 2025 were added later, where appropriate.","rect":[49.5,606.7770000000002,367.06505000000016,616.2770000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"STRUCTURE:","rect":[49.5,587.7770000000002,89.87405000000001,597.2770000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"This guideline represents the most current and comprehensive evidence available in AIS care. Key updates include the","rect":[91.775,587.7770000000002,535.4534999999996,597.2770000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"incorporation of new evidence related to thrombolytic choice and eligibility, determination of eligibility for endovascular thrombectomy,","rect":[49.50000000000001,576.7760000000002,535.4724999999993,586.2760000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"and management of hyperglycemia and dysphagia; a focused consideration of the pediatric population; and modification of","rect":[49.50000000000001,565.7750000000002,535.5009999999995,575.2750000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"the approach to thrombolysis contraindications. Although this guideline reflects significant advances, it also highlights gaps in","rect":[49.50000000000001,554.7740000000002,535.5389999999992,564.2740000000002],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"knowledge and underscores the urgent need for continued research to further refine and improve treatment strategies.","rect":[49.50000000000001,543.7730000000003,496.9119999999998,553.2730000000003],"fontSize":9.5},{"text":"Key Words:","rect":[77.631,519.895,111.957,528.895],"fontSize":9},{"text":"AHA Scientific Statements","rect":[114.2067,520.115,203.55070000000003,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"◼","rect":[205.7187,520.115,211.2707,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"endovascular procedures","rect":[213.4387,520.115,296.9587,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"◼","rect":[299.1267000000001,520.115,304.6787000000001,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"guideline","rect":[306.8467000000001,520.115,337.0147000000001,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"◼","rect":[339.1827000000001,520.115,344.73470000000015,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"ischemic stroke","rect":[346.90270000000015,520.115,398.91070000000013,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"◼","rect":[401.07870000000014,520.115,406.63070000000016,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"stroke","rect":[408.79870000000017,520.115,429.63870000000014,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"◼","rect":[431.8067000000002,520.115,437.3587000000002,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"thrombolytic therapy","rect":[439.52670000000023,520.115,507.37470000000025,528.115],"fontSize":8},{"text":"TABLE OF CONTENTS","rect":[49.5,467.015,168.96869999999996,480.015],"fontSize":13},{"text":"Top Take-Home Messages","rect":[49.5,447.675,160.37,457.675],"fontSize":10},{"text":". . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .","rect":[163.377,447.675,257.02700000000016,457.675],"fontSize":10},{"text":"e","rect":[260.8003,447.675,266.0103,457.675],"fontSize":10},{"text":"318","rect":[266.0103,447.675,283.5003,457.675],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Abstract","rect":[49.50030000000001,435.675,84.5103,445.675],"fontSize":10},{"text":". . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .","rect":[84.5395,435.675,257.0295000000002